{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling","id":1479200,"title":"So \"The Howling\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-20T17:56:10-07:00","id":1479200,"title":"So \"The Howling\"","content":"What would the werewolves of &quot;The Howling&quot; be? A bunch of horny Fianna? Some relatively sane Black Spiral Dancers? A Glass Walker or Child of Gaia psychiatrist's failed attempt at controlling the more violent werewolf tendencies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T18:04:40-07:00","id":1479201,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been a really long time since I\u2019ve seen The Holwing movies, but from what I recall Black Spiral Dancers seem appropriate.<br /> <br /> Except for The Howling III, they would be Bunyips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T20:58:13-07:00","id":1479210,"title":"","content":"The hardest part of this would be how to factor in how The Howling (at least the first movie) really relies on the spread by biting. Even if you expand out the time scale, too many plot beats don't really fit with how WtA structures werewolves.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to The Colony from The Howling is probably the Valkenburg Foundation: the residents are Lunatics, each with their own issues and personalities, as they have no organizing principles or philosophies. Perhaps a version run by someone less well meaning than the Stargazers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T23:12:36-07:00","id":1479211,"title":"","content":"If I were to do the Howling in a chronicle, I would run them as Ronin with the character of Dr Waggner attempting to cure or control their affliction (their Rage). But Eddie Quist (and his sister Marsha) would be falling to the Wyrm, and an obvious candidate for recruitment by the Black Spiral Dancers or possibly have already been approached. Dr Waggner might possibly be an actual Child of Gaia attempting to integrate Ronin into his tribe, or at least exposed to them.<br /> <br /> Most Werewolf movies are only going to match their characters to Ronin (or Lunatics) because the particulars of the Garou depart to much from pop culture werewolves.<br /> <br /> While I think the Howling is a very dated movie, it has a lot of elements I love. And I work hard to have my setting be able to emulate the movie in some capacity. It's one reason I increase the population of Ronin to a much higher number than is official. Maybe something like 10-25% of all Garou are Ronin in my setting - making them the largest &quot;tribe&quot; bigger than either the BSDs or Bone Gnawers. There's just too much cool pop culture werewolf stuff that can only be done through them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T00:24:07-07:00","id":1479216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479211#post1479211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most Werewolf movies are only going to match their characters to Ronin (or Lunatics) because the particulars of the Garou depart to much from pop culture werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and it is to WtA's detriment. While Dog Soldiers clearly are a BSD pack (Scotland, human larder), most movie werewolf stories really only work if the werewolf is not tied to any authority but themselves.<br /> <br /> Plotlines such as a family of ronin ruling a small town how they wish is great stuff because it removes all the tribal fluff and just focuses on what the garou can do if given free rein from Gaias or the Wyrm. Something the books never really dwell on, focusing solely on how -lonely- the ronin are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T13:33:35-07:00","id":1479367,"title":"","content":"The Howling is hard to classify for WtA. It's a very Forsaken movie to me. The pack , the need for death, kill, sex and so on. <br /> <br /> If we go wta, I would say, DrWaggner some kind of visionary (and little insane) Silver Fang, I would go Red Talons for Marsha, Eddie and the other brother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T03:24:38-07:00","id":1479878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479216#post1479216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dog Soldiers clearly are a BSD pack (Scotland, human larder)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't agree with you. I once used this movie as an inspiration for my game. I started with politician and military caste from 7th Generation and the general from Warriors of the Apocalypse. They deliberately send soldiers to the areas they suspect the caern is (especially in places outside US, where US Army operates, like Middle East). If Garou react with fury the soldiers will die, most of the survivors will be subject to Delirium and caern defenders will be weaken. Then they can send BSD to finish the job or let the Air Force accidentally drop the bombs there (you know, some maps are inaccurate etc. \ud83d\ude08). Also SAD knows that many of the shapeshifters come from Native Americans, German and Irish population. So I think that werewolves from Dog Soldiers can be from any tribe BUT BSD.<br /> <br /> I also strongly reccomend a 1993 HBO movie, Full Eclipse, with Mario van Peebles, Bruce Payne and Patsy Kensit (which was once also my inspiration). Imagine the main bad guy as a BSD who remained quite sane (as for BSD, being a honest cop helped, just like it is said in Robocop II about Murphy). He just become more fanatical. I remember my player's faces when they meet him and his fomori buddies (one of the characters was a made man). On one side he truly made the streets safer, he could even agree to leave mentioned made man gang intact (and even help him get rid of competitors) on certain terms (no drugs for minorities, no racketeering, no theft and robbery, no forced prostitution, always leave some money for gamblers and never accept anything that hard cash from them, basically everything that leaves the &quot;civilians&quot; unharmed). On the other hand the Litany: fight the Wyrm wherever it breeds. Alternatively you could use a GW making his fellow cops Drones but I doubt it would give the same impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-01-2022, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T03:44:10-07:00","id":1479880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479878#post1479878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't agree with you. I once used this movie as an inspiration for my game. I started with politician and military caste from 7th Generation and the general from Warriors of the Apocalypse. They deliberately send soldiers to the areas they suspect the caern is (especially in places outside US, where US Army operates, like Middle East). If Garou react with fury the soldiers will die, most of the survivors will be subject to Delirium and caern defenders will be weaken. Then they can send BSD to finish the job or let the Air Force accidentally drop the bombs there (you know, some maps are inaccurate etc. \ud83d\ude08). Also SAD knows that many of the shapeshifters come from Native Americans, German and Irish population. So I think that werewolves from Dog Soldiers can be from any tribe BUT BSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are Bone Gnawer Man-Eaters, BSDs are basically the only tribe they can be to me. Since the Litany forbids eating human flesh and this is one law most garou are VERY adamant about, the larder full of human parts in the house the werewolves live in would be an automatic Litany Breach and a fast track to Wyrm Taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T04:03:43-07:00","id":1479883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479880#post1479880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless they are Bone Gnawer Man-Eaters, BSDs are basically the only tribe they can be to me. Since the Litany forbids eating human flesh and this is one law most garou are VERY adamant about, the larder full of human parts in the house the werewolves live in would be an automatic Litany Breach and a fast track to Wyrm Taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>So don't stick to this image. Ok, in that you're right but what if...<br /> Also they could also be a branch of Dunsirn family, unclaimed by Giovanni, so they could easily be Fianna. Also if you set this in Appalachia they could be Dunsirn Fianna/Bone Gnawers Man Eaters mountaineers. Add one Silent Strider's Eater of the Dead and one or two Skin Dancers and you'll have a quite interesting sept. Maybe some of them could be &quot;recycled&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":".  Some more insane ideas 05-01-2022, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T04:28:15-07:00","id":1479885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479883#post1479883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So don't stick to this image. Ok, in that you're right but what if...<br /> Also they could also be a branch of Dunsirn family, unclaimed by Giovanni, so they could easily be Fianna. Also if you set this in Appalachia they could be Dunsirn Fianna/Bone Gnawers Man Eaters mountaineers. Add one Silent Strider's Eater of the Dead and one or two Skin Dancers and you'll have a quite interesting sept. Maybe some of them could be &quot;recycled&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just how I see it, and you are absolutely entitled to your own takes, but the location and the behaviour of the werewolves makes them a perfect BSD family for me. Not only due to their num num humans thing, but also how casual they are about it. These garou just casually have a cabin in the middle of the woods where they eat human soup and live their best life.<br /> <br /> Them being BSDs adds a really nice feeling of dread, because it is one thing to run into a Gaian pack. It is ENTIRELY another to run into a BSD one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T10:29:50-07:00","id":1479901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479885#post1479885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just how I see it, and you are absolutely entitled to your own takes, but the location and the behaviour of the werewolves makes them a perfect BSD family for me. Not only due to their num num humans thing, but also how casual they are about it. These garou just casually have a cabin in the middle of the woods where they eat human soup and live their best life.<br /> <br /> Them being BSDs adds a really nice feeling of dread, because it is one thing to run into a Gaian pack. It is ENTIRELY another to run into a BSD one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course BSD gives the feeling of dread. But I prefere the feeling of moral relativity and choices of conscience rather during my games. The way I see it: if it was a BSD pack the thing is simple: fight the Wyrm wherever it breeds. But if it was a Gaian pack, especially if they are all outcasts (as I described it, Bone Gnawer with an 8-ball around his neck, Dunsirn Fianna/Ronin who was omited by Giovanni, lost and lonely Skin Dancer who undergo the rite but couldn't handle the consequences and knowledge obsessed Eater of the Dead) could be a different thing. Imagine them without the Wyrm taint (ok, maybe not Skin Dancer). Add a dormant Wyrm caern of Lust nearby which they discovered. They are too weak to open it and cannot go to any sept for help because of their reputation. Was it the caern that twisted them or maybe they were insane from the beginning. Maybe eating people is their way to keep mortals away from that place. Maybe this caerm can be cleansed and return to its original function, to be the caern of Fertility, one of the rarest caern type. If so then what about them? They won't give it for free. What would be their price. Or maybe they found an unclaimed Fertility caern and turned it to a caern of Lust. Maybe if you search the basement you will find a metis or two, still untainted. Of course it would be for a game where PCs are Gaian pack. On the other hand a group of mortals finding such metis could easily lead to an ET style game.<br /> <br /> Of course if I have to stick to the original plot, where PCs are soldiers from the movie I would use BSD too.<br /> <br /> And of course there's no need to assume that larder full of body parts means automaticaly that they eat human flesh. Maybe it's just for psychological effect. Maybe it's rather a trophy room. Like with the Red Talons, you can find human body parts nearby but that doesn't mean they eat them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-01-2022, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T16:34:40-07:00","id":1480060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479878#post1479878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also strongly reccomend a 1993 HBO movie, Full Eclipse, with Mario van Peebles, Bruce Payne and Patsy Kensit (which was once also my inspiration).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of this movie so I had to look it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z6suPmglqsI\" data-code=\"z6suPmglqsI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/z6suPmglqsI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is so ridiculously awesome I can't believe I never heard of this until now. The change between originally thinking its some vigilante action movie to something about werewolves is so jarring I find it very amusing. At the same time, this is so in tune with what I expect from the World of Darkness that it is natural. I imagine if the trailer was cut differently, it'd be less jarring and amusing. I have to find out where to view the entire movie now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1479880#post1479880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they are Bone Gnawer Man-Eaters, BSDs are basically the only tribe they can be to me. Since the Litany forbids eating human flesh and this is one law most garou are VERY adamant about, the larder full of human parts in the house the werewolves live in would be an automatic Litany Breach and a fast track to Wyrm Taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles, I treat man eating in a similar way as drug abuse. In the general Garou population, about 5% of Garou have eaten people in the past five years, and 1% are pretty hard core ongoing eaters. Overall, there's probably 10-15% of Garou who have done it at some point in their lives. Incidents are probably higher among the Ronin.<br /> <br /> Now some of those Garou only did so by accident, or just once or a few times and never did so again. (It frequently happens with First Changers/Lost Cubs before the Garou find them and teach them how to control it.) But it's done enough that the crime is in the Litany for a reason. The notorious camps like the Man Eaters, Eaters of the Dead, and other canonical groups make up most of the 1% who do so continuously. But the rest is spread throughout the Garou tribes. The difference between being an addict who needs help and an internal enemy that needs to be destroyed mostly depends on whether they justify it (like the Man Eaters and Eaters of the Dead do) or admit they have a problem.<br /> <br /> The Garou break their own law just as much as there is crime in any human society. Most Garou follow the law. They aren't hypocrites. But there's always a criminal element of varying degrees. And most of their criminals don't become traitors. Just because they break one or more precepts of the Litany doesn't mean they're falling to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I like a certain amount of &quot;normal&quot; criminal behavior that results in Philodoxes actually using the Rites of Punishment in the sept. Otherwise the Philodox have a lot less to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T22:40:05-07:00","id":1480079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480060#post1480060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never heard of this movie so I had to look it up.<br /> <br /> This is so ridiculously awesome I can't believe I never heard of this until now. The change between originally thinking its some vigilante action movie to something about werewolves is so jarring I find it very amusing. At the same time, this is so in tune with what I expect from the World of Darkness that it is natural. I imagine if the trailer was cut differently, it'd be less jarring and amusing. I have to find out where to view the entire movie now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest it is a vigilante cop action movie but with a great WoD atmosphere and werewolves. 2 funny things:<br /> 1. Look at the shapeshift scene near the end of the movie (little spoiler alert). It's not a slow, painful process &quot;because of full moon&quot; or &quot;because it's your curse&quot; (like in &quot;The Wolf&quot; with Nicholson, another great werewolf movie). It looks like &quot;I spend a Rage point and attack&quot;.<br /> 2. In 1st Edition Get of Fenris tribebook there's a Ragabash vigilante cop template.<br /> And another fun fact: I've never seen trailer of this movie. A friend of mine got this movie on videotape in mid 90s and that's how it begun. <br /> <br /> I may also recommend you another old movie, Wolfen, with Albert Finney, Tom Noonan, Tom Waits and Diane Venora. It's a quasi film noir about &quot;werewolves&quot; (they aren't shown on the screen). It was even mentioned in &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon&quot; adventure/sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T23:41:18-07:00","id":1480081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480079#post1480079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may also recommend you another old movie, Wolfen, with Albert Finney, Tom Noonan, Tom Waits and Diane Venora.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've both seen the movie Wolfen and read the book (by Whitley Strieber). There are major differences between the two, but the movie is clearly based on the book and not just &quot;inspired&quot; by it. I don't remember Tom Waits in it. I do remember Edward James Olmos.<br /> <br /> Strieber was an important horror author in the late seventies and early eighties with his popular books Wolfen and the Hunger which &quot;updated&quot; the vampire and werewolf myths to be more &quot;realistic&quot;. Less supernatural and more alternative forms of life. But he's mostly forgotten today except for the UFO crowd which got into his non-fiction (but crazy) books on abductions like Communion.<br /> <br /> Wolfen certainly has a lot of things I steal for my chronicles. One can arguably base a lot of Red Talon stuff on it (though in the movie which brings a lot of Native American stuff which is not in the actual book, it might be better to explain them as lupus of the Wendigo tribe). Plus that James Horner score (the same guy who did the score for Star Trek II: Wrath of Khan) is just awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u_EJkbC3lf8\" data-code=\"u_EJkbC3lf8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u_EJkbC3lf8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=weYGiULosmE\" data-code=\"weYGiULosmE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/weYGiULosmE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 1981 is probably the peak year for werewolf movies with the Howling, American Werewolf in London, and Wolfen. All three are big inspirations for me. I feel I must be able to simulate those movies (if not duplicate them exactly) in some fashion, or I'm not getting the genre right. They're up there for me as Werewolf of London and the Wolfman. I haven't seen the Curse of the Werewolf (Hammer film starring Oliver Reed, based on Guy Endore's Werewolf of Paris which is supposed to be the closest equivalent of Dracula for werewolves) yet. I also want to see Ginger Snaps which looks awesome and would probably be great to steal from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-04-2022, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T00:24:48-07:00","id":1480082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480079#post1480079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(like in &quot;The Wolf&quot; with Nicholson, another great werewolf movie)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like 1994's Wolf, but I think it's just OK as opposed to awesome. But there's a lot I steal from it. I love the idea that Nicholson's character could be a Lost Cub. Although it has lots of precedents, this is the movie that cemented the idea in my mind that a Garou biting a Lost Cub could help bring about the First Change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4ZZ-Es9olys\" data-code=\"4ZZ-Es9olys\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4ZZ-Es9olys/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I also like the changes in behavior in Nicholson before the change and afterwards. I try to incorporate it with how I play Garou NPCs versus normal humans. Unfortunately when I focus on plot, I tend to forget this. The interaction between Nicholson and Spader is great. This is an obvious scene, but there are many great moments of the two trying to establish dominance - a very human trait as well as a wolf one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ItgJzRKo2WI\" data-code=\"ItgJzRKo2WI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ItgJzRKo2WI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And this scene does a good job of explaining the positive aspects of being Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ys-c3gmcEQQ\" data-code=\"ys-c3gmcEQQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ys-c3gmcEQQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Wolf doesn't quite come together as a supernatural or horror movie for me. But there's lots of things to like, and good inspiration for the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T02:38:51-07:00","id":1480085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480060#post1480060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my chronicles, I treat man eating in a similar way as drug abuse. In the general Garou population, about 5% of Garou have eaten people in the past five years, and 1% are pretty hard core ongoing eaters. Overall, there's probably 10-15% of Garou who have done it at some point in their lives. Incidents are probably higher among the Ronin.<br /> <br /> Now some of those Garou only did so by accident, or just once or a few times and never did so again. (It frequently happens with First Changers/Lost Cubs before the Garou find them and teach them how to control it.) But it's done enough that the crime is in the Litany for a reason. The notorious camps like the Man Eaters, Eaters of the Dead, and other canonical groups make up most of the 1% who do so continuously. But the rest is spread throughout the Garou tribes. The difference between being an addict who needs help and an internal enemy that needs to be destroyed mostly depends on whether they justify it (like the Man Eaters and Eaters of the Dead do) or admit they have a problem.<br /> <br /> The Garou break their own law just as much as there is crime in any human society. Most Garou follow the law. They aren't hypocrites. But there's always a criminal element of varying degrees. And most of their criminals don't become traitors. Just because they break one or more precepts of the Litany doesn't mean they're falling to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I like a certain amount of &quot;normal&quot; criminal behavior that results in Philodoxes actually using the Rites of Punishment in the sept. Otherwise the Philodox have a lot less to do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally do think this happens at times, First Change being common. But the playerbase I play with is close enough to their kinfolk and human side that I don't think it would work with them. There just isn't as much of a disconnect between human and garou to justify it not being seen as a Great Horror.<br /> <br /> Mind, Red Talons and some Ronin communities definitely do engage in willing cannibalism in my HC. Red Talons because they do not accept the Litany as written and the Ronin because that's what werewolves do, right?<br /> <br /> Also, agreed on Wolf being a good example of garou vs human behaviour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T06:36:45-07:00","id":1480091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480082#post1480082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea that Nicholson's character could be a Lost Cub. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I call this movie great.<br /> <br /> First of all the gradually change in Nicholson's character, from an older guy, who's health is failing and who is loosing his will to fight into an alpha male. That includes:<br /> -marking of the teritory you've mentioned<br /> -heightened senses (&quot;don't tell me it was a drop of tequilla&quot;)<br /> -(yeah, I know, feminists will lynch me \ud83d\ude09) his male sexual energy<br /> Plus the devilish smile of Nicholson so no characterisation was needed. The same changes in Spader who reacts differently. And, IMHO, the worst part: Michelle Pfeiffer. Don't get me wrong, I think she starred many great movies but it's hard to get some emotions from her. It worked in &quot;Scarface&quot; but as a she-wolf she's too calm. <br /> <br /> As for inspiration I used this movie to put a new player to my group. The pack was the Questing Pack for Valkenburg Foundation. They found the new character struggling for control (the player didn't know what game he'll be playing, he only knew that the setting will be modern and I tried hard to convince him that his character becomes psychotic) and bring him to the Foundation. Then one day I run a one player story for him (the therapy) and another for the pack who tried to cover their tracks from new guy's family on one hand and on the other tried to find out if they are Kinfolks (they weren't, he was an effect of his mother's romance). But at the same time his father was gradually slipping into Wyrm services as an Omni TV employee. In the end, when the Foundation staff agreed for a meeting, the new guy face the same choice as Nicholson: either he will return to human society (they will supress his nature with a fetish) or accept his nature and help his parents. As the player was convinced that he will play Call of Cthulhu (he told me so afterwards) and thought that becoming a werewolf was unnatural it worked perfectly.<br /> <br /> As for Wolfen I didn't read the book but I saw the movie after I read about it in &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon&quot;. I like the idea of cop becoming a hunter. I liked the character played by Noonan fascinated by wolves. And those statistics they've mentioned, about lots of homeless people who disappear every year without a trace.<br /> <br /> I also forgot about Teenage Werewolf. Ok, some may find it silly but I like the idea of an average teenager who suddenly discovers what he is capable of. On one hand he can become a sport star of his school and win the lead cheerleader heart (or at least other body parts \ud83d\ude1c) on the other hand there's a sept who try to convince him not to do that. And what if there wasn't any sept? Or they weren't aware of the cub? Add this cub (NPC) a Fair Glabro merit (maybe noone in his school notice the change because of that) and then make him shift into crinos during the final match. And then let the PCs clean this mess (maybe with Damage Control so possibly a Mage crossover here).<br /> <br /> IwaI'miting for your review of &quot;Full eclipse&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T06:49:05-07:00","id":1480092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480085#post1480085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally do think this happens at times, First Change being common. But the playerbase I play with is close enough to their kinfolk and human side that I don't think it would work with them. There just isn't as much of a disconnect between human and garou to justify it not being seen as a Great Horror.<br /> <br /> Mind, Red Talons and some Ronin communities definitely do engage in willing cannibalism in my HC. Red Talons because they do not accept the Litany as written and the Ronin because that's what werewolves do, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I begun to wonder what the Elder Philodox would say about a garou who survived the 1972 Flight 571 crash. Ok, some may say that he could bring help going through the Umbra or something like that but what if it was homid, who was severely wounded (regeneration doesn't put your bones in proper place, it just heals them as they are), had low Gnosis or was just afraid of spirit world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T07:40:30-07:00","id":1480094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480092#post1480092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I begun to wonder what the Elder Philodox would say about a garou who survived the 1972 Flight 571 crash. Ok, some may say that he could bring help going through the Umbra or something like that but what if it was homid, who was severely wounded (regeneration doesn't put your bones in proper place, it just heals them as they are), had low Gnosis or was just afraid of spirit world?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, regen does fix your bones correctly. It is magic after all.<br /> <br /> There are two types of answers to that question; One of a rited garou and one of First Change.<br /> <br /> For the rited garou, the first question would be why would they have not just taken their crinos form and left. Even without using the umbra, the crinos form has fur and +4 strength and +3 stamina. Nevermind any gifts they might have. So I'd say they would be seen as a willing cannibal.<br /> <br /> For the First Change, there would be much more leeway. Though given how long the people stayed there (unless the cub killed them all), they would be looked with suspicion of taint.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T08:17:35-07:00","id":1480097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480094#post1480094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, regen does fix your bones correctly. It is magic after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 p.260, Battle Scars: &quot;one of your character's bones snapped and did not heal properly&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480094#post1480094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the rited garou, the first question would be why would they have not just taken their crinos form and left. Even without using the umbra, the crinos form has fur and +4 strength and +3 stamina. Nevermind any gifts they might have. So I'd say they would be seen as a willing cannibal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it was a Children of Gaia and couldn't leave the humans (not to mention that loosing Renown for leaving the helpless humans behind). Or maybe its physical stats and survival skills (any of them, survival is obvious, athletics for climbing etc.) are abysmal (take the worst combination, that would give him 5 strenght and 4 stamina in CRINOS form; I saw that combination once) so going anywhere was beyond its capabilities (not to mention that if you fall asleep you return to your natural from and spending the night above 11000 ft having strenght and stamina 1 is not a very bright idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T08:58:24-07:00","id":1480100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480097#post1480097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 p.260, Battle Scars: &quot;one of your character's bones snapped and did not heal properly&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Battle Scars happen when the character hits incap. Otherwise, things heal as normal. Battle Scars are when the healing FAILS to do its job due to the character almost dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480097#post1480097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it was a Children of Gaia and couldn't leave the humans (not to mention that loosing Renown for leaving the helpless humans behind). Or maybe its physical stats and survival skills (any of them, survival is obvious, athletics for climbing etc.) are abysmal (take the worst combination, that would give him 5 strenght and 4 stamina in CRINOS form; I saw that combination once) so going anywhere was beyond its capabilities (not to mention that if you fall asleep you return to your natural from and spending the night above 11000 ft having strenght and stamina 1 is not a very bright idea).</div> </div> </div> </div>5 strength is still the human maximum, far beyond what the stranded people would have had. Nevermind 4 stamina is ALMOST the maximum for humans. Plus Rage and gifts.<br /> <br /> Also, there is nothing in the book saying that you return to your birth form when you sleep. People just house rule it due to the knockout rules.<br /> <br /> Regardless, a rited garou is expected to not succumb to the Wyrm. No matter how unfair the situation the sept would be asking why the garou didn't just hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-04-2022, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T09:28:15-07:00","id":1480101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480100#post1480100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Battle Scars happen when the character hits incap. Otherwise, things heal as normal. Battle Scars are when the healing FAILS to do its job due to the character almost dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I belive that you quote 2nd edition in which Battle Scars can be aquire twofold:<br /> 1. If a garou reach health level incapacitated then the roll is made for battle scar<br /> 2. If the Rage roll for staying active while being critically wounded fails then the roll is made for battle scar adding one die.<br /> In W20 it's storyteller's discretion. i believe that a plane crash is a good cause of battle scar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480100#post1480100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 strength is still the human maximum, far beyond what the stranded people would have had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. But it would have it only in crinos from. And, as there was a professional sport team on board, it could be one of the many with stamina 4 (which I believe is more important than strenght 5). Hell, I once participated in Cooper's test during high school. Without proper training I run about 2 miles in 12 minutes. It means that my result was as good as an average junior pro or on the top of average human capabilities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480100#post1480100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there is nothing in the book saying that you return to your birth form when you sleep. People just house rule it due to the knockout rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't agree with you. While you're right about the knock out (or death) rules I think you forgot 3 things :<br /> 1. Basically knock out is when you can't control your body. Sleep is basically similar in that. As remaining in chosen form requires control sleeping should induce return to breeds form<br /> 2. In most of the novels sleeping characters return to their breed forms.<br /> 3. There was said that as garou can use all five forms the most comfortable is its breed form. As most of the living things search comfort for their sleep it should also apply to garou taking breed form during their sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-04-2022, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T09:47:59-07:00","id":1480104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480100#post1480100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, a rited garou is expected to not succumb to the Wyrm. No matter how unfair the situation the sept would be asking why the garou didn't just hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I know there was only one kind of prey: humans. Remember that it was above 11000 ft (3500 m), well over the snow line. And there aren't many animals living on that level. So basically mentioned Garou could either hunt (and eat) humans or rely on roadkill (airkill?). I think that it's not succumbing to the Wyrm (especially it wasn't the habit but an adaptation to the extreme situation). Rather a survival of the fittest. If that is the same then succumbing to the Wyrm I pity the entire Garou race \ud83d\ude09.<br /> <br /> And it's not the only situation when people (and possibly Garou) eat human flesh. Remember the great famine (Hlomodor &quot;to kill by starvation&quot;) in early 30's in Ukraine. A little off topic: do you think that it would generate some kind of spirit which still exists today and Garou could lead an epic attack on it? And how powerful it could be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-04-2022, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T10:24:43-07:00","id":1480108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480104#post1480104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I know there was only one kind of prey: humans. Remember that it was above 11000 ft (3500 m), well over the snow line. And there aren't many animals living on that level. So basically mentioned Garou could either hunt (and eat) humans or rely on roadkill (airkill?). I think that it's not succumbing to the Wyrm (especially it wasn't the habit but an adaptation to the extreme situation). Rather a survival of the fittest. If that is the same then succumbing to the Wyrm I pity the entire Garou race \ud83d\ude09.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, there aren't. The point I'm trying to make is that the (rited) garou would be expected to be -better- than eating human flesh. Basically, most tribes would expect the garou to leave the humans and get to safety. Maybe then bring aid to the humans if they feel the need to. Staying in homid and joining in cannibalism when they have other options available would not be seen favourably. Even if they were 1 str 1 stam, they still would have access to crinos, hispo and lupus to leave safely.<br /> <br /> Even with a broken leg, even with a collapsed lung. There are garou who drag themselves on their front paws if need be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T11:16:04-07:00","id":1480111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480108#post1480108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, there aren't. The point I'm trying to make is that the (rited) garou would be expected to be -better- than eating human flesh. Basically, most tribes would expect the garou to leave the humans and get to safety. Maybe then bring aid to the humans if they feel the need to. Staying in homid and joining in cannibalism when they have other options available would not be seen favourably. Even if they were 1 str 1 stam, they still would have access to crinos, hispo and lupus to leave safely.<br /> <br /> Even with a broken leg, even with a collapsed lung. There are garou who drag themselves on their front paws if need be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So let's try to decide which tribes would judge mentioned Garou harsh and which would accept it as some necessity. My turn<br /> Punishement: Fianna, Get of Fenris, Silent Striders, Silver Fangs, Wendigo<br /> Acceptance: Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Stargazers, Shadow Lords, Uktena, Glass Walkers.<br /> I omitted Red Talons. Not just because they have a special place in their hearts for humans but also because I have trouble imagining one of them in a plane. My call is that it would be rather 50:50.<br /> <br /> As for other options available it's not so simple. First of all they would rather be homids and most of the survival advices tell you to stay in the place of crash so the rescue team could easily find you. So IMO most of the homids would stay. Second some of the survivors went for help after a few days when they learned that the search was cancelled. Third...<br /> <br /> And that's when I get the idea for an adventure. Most likely none of the survivors would let the garou walk alone so no shapeshift would be possible. Second as it was above the snow line tracking would be nearly impossible so such Garou have to either know the navigation techniques based on stars or ask the pilot which route would be the best (just as the survivors did). Let's say that the survivors noticed the character missing even if he survived the crash. No body was found. He went alone. When they followed him (the pilot told them which way to go) they found only wolf tracks. After 50 years some DNA guy accidentally found this raport about one person missing after the crash and the wolf tracks. He begin the investigation. Now this Garou is a respected Elder of a prominent urban caern and lives in the city under his own human name. And all of the sudden DNA teams arrives and begin the hunt. During the climax PCs learn that it was the Elder's past that stomp onto them. Will they hide this fact or will they accuse him of lifting the Veil (even if it was 50 years ago; do Garou have statute of limitations) and endangering the caern?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T11:30:57-07:00","id":1480112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480111#post1480111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other options available it's not so simple. First of all they would rather be homids and most of the survival advices tell you to stay in the place of crash so the rescue team could easily find you. So IMO most of the homids would stay. Second some of the survivors went for help after a few days when they learned that the search was cancelled. Third...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they stick to homid form when they have 3 much better forms to survive in? And all three forms have regeneration and fur on top of everything, negating a lot of the dangers the situation has.<br /> <br /> Yes, survival experts say to stay in one place for -humans-, but I imagine a magical shapeshifting reality travelling werewolf with the minimum of the peak of the human condition would fare a bit better in searching for safety.<br /> <br /> If the regular humans eventually, after starving for a good while, made a trek to safety I'd say a garou with crinos form would do that with way more ease.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T11:31:18-07:00","id":1480113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480085#post1480085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally do think this happens at times, First Change being common. But the playerbase I play with is close enough to their kinfolk and human side that I don't think it would work with them. There just isn't as much of a disconnect between human and garou to justify it not being seen as a Great Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, PCs will likely never engage in man eating unless one has an unusual character concept, backstory, or personal plot they're pursuing. It's just something I use for the NPCs on a general level. <br /> <br /> For many septs, it's not something I bother with at all. But sometimes I'll decide that 1 or 2 members of some sept are secret man eaters (or some other crime). Sometimes it's just background description that doesn't mean anything (OK, you travel to the next step to share the news, and you learn that one of its members have recently been ostracized after being discovered to have eaten someone). That adds some flavor to the game, and very often causes the PCs to engage more with the NPCs. Or it's a sandbox element the PCs could discover and be the ones to bring that Garou to justice. But these crimes are incidental along the same lines of discovering a friend, coworker, or family member was secretly a meth addict.<br /> <br /> The organized groups of Man Eaters are more like the criminal gangs that peddle the drugs. I limit them to the usual suspects and as intended chronicle plots. I really liked the character of Bone Juice in Rage Across New York, and wanted to see additional NPCs like that in other Rage books (like Mother Pasta in Australia). So I often include some group of deviants somewhere in the chronicle that could be discovered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T11:57:01-07:00","id":1480115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480112#post1480112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they stick to homid form when they have 3 much better forms to survive in? And all three forms have regeneration and fur on top of everything, negating a lot of the dangers the situation has.<br /> <br /> Yes, survival experts say to stay in one place for -humans-, but I imagine a magical shapeshifting reality travelling werewolf with the minimum of the peak of the human condition would fare a bit better in searching for safety.<br /> <br /> If the regular humans eventually, after starving for a good while, made a trek to safety I'd say a garou with crinos form would do that with way more ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. But look at the adventure idea I wrote. How they would explain their sudden missing (their names are most likely on passengers list) and what would be the implications of that. As for being in peak of human condition it's the most optimistic variant. More likely they would be wounded (even if the regeneration worked which also be hard to explain). Of course most of the Garou live in packs and most of the packs have totem. So they could easily alarm their packmates and bring help. If the entire pack was on that plane well &quot;no one but us will know&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T12:07:37-07:00","id":1480116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480115#post1480115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. But look at the adventure idea I wrote. How they would explain their sudden missing (their names are most likely on passengers list) and what would be the implications of that. As for being in peak of human condition it's the most optimistic variant. More likely they would be wounded (even if the regeneration worked which also be hard to explain). Of course most of the Garou live in packs and most of the packs have totem. So they could easily alarm their packmates and bring help. If the entire pack was on that plane well &quot;no one but us will know&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Delirium or gifts would handle the 'missing person' issue. If not, then I feel most garou would go underground/change names for a good while.<br /> <br /> This is also assuming the garou did not murder everyone in their Rage Up frenzy. Which would go more towards your adventure, since that is much harder to explain.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T12:27:07-07:00","id":1480117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480113#post1480113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The organized groups of Man Eaters are more like the criminal gangs that peddle the drugs. I limit them to the usual suspects and as intended chronicle plots. I really liked the character of Bone Juice in Rage Across New York, and wanted to see additional NPCs like that in other Rage books (like Mother Pasta in Australia). So I often include some group of deviants somewhere in the chronicle that could be discovered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once used the template of maneater from &quot;Outcasts&quot;. I gave it to my best player (to be my First Mate, but later the PCs pack accepted him) and it worked great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T12:32:06-07:00","id":1480119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480116#post1480116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Delirium or gifts would handle the 'missing person' issue. If not, then I feel most garou would go underground/change names for a good while.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it won't. Delirium makes mortals forget crinos or rationalize it (&quot;it wasn't werewolf, these were terrorists&quot;) not forget about Garou in homid. The most optimistic version would be that such terrorists killed him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480116#post1480116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also assuming the garou did not murder everyone in their Rage Up frenzy. Which would go more towards your adventure, since that is much harder to explain.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's another thing. And I agree that it would be hard to explain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T12:45:33-07:00","id":1480121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480092#post1480092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I begun to wonder what the Elder Philodox would say about a garou who survived the 1972 Flight 571 crash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannibalism is taboo in most human cultures and regarded with fear and horror. At the same time, people also understand the concept of survival cannibalism - when isolated people without sufficient food can either die of starvation, or eat some of the remains of the dead to survive. While still regarded as horrific and tragic, people who resorted to survival cannibalism are treated differently than people who killed other people in order to eat them for reasons that don't have to do with survival.<br /> <br /> While a Garou has sufficient powers to avoid survival cannibalism in many cases, we can always figure out a scenario where he may still need to resort to it. If so, I think most Garou would still treat cases of survival cannibalism differently than in other cases.<br /> <br /> Of course, much depends on the tribal and sept culture. The Falcon totem has extremely high standards, and if you are in a tribe, sept, or pack that follows Falcon, there is going to be punishment, maybe at the same level as intentional man eating. But what if it is Rat or Cockroach - totems often associated with surviving at all costs? There may not be anything. Other spirits might be something in-between - a lesser rite of punishment used like ostracism for a month to contemplate and atone for his crimes, and then nobody mentions it again and everyone moves on.<br /> <br /> = =<br /> In most chronicles I've played in, there's very little mundane crimes. It's either no crimes at all, or if they happen it's because someone is falling to the Wyrm and on the verge of becoming a traitor.<br /> <br /> I like to see more things in-between those two extremes. There are a lot of Punishment Rites out there. Unless they get used, they are just kind of useless. They exist only as flavor text. And it can be hard for players to earn Honor Renown. Having more &quot;petty&quot; crimes gives PCs a chance to use those Rites, investigate crimes, and so on that earn them Honor. Now you don't want those crimes to get out of hand and dominate the game. They should be limited and spread around a lot of different septs.<br /> <br /> But there should be a small criminal element among the Garou just like there is to humans, and a large percentage of them won't get to the point of falling to the Wyrm. There will be Garou who will trespass, cheat, steal, embezzle, murder, engage in the occasional man eating, mate with another Garou, rape, vandalize, assault, destroy property, commit sacrilege, or something else. It might be accidental, done under the influence of drugs or alcohol, intentional, or done repeatedly. Some of the lesser crimes might just be at the level of Renown loss, but others will lead to Punishment Rites that fall short of The Hunt or Gaia's Vengeful Teeth.<br /> <br /> So I don't believe that the Garou don't violate the Litany at all. Some do, and it isn't because they serve the Wyrm. It's still criminal behavior, but they're not traitors. They are just lawbreakers. So one of my generic rules in designing a setting is to have around 5% of the NPCs be someone who is committing some kind of crime against the Litany. So I'll figure out which two Garou are committing an illicit love affair. Which one steals fetishes or talens as crimes of opportunity. Which one visits another sept or pack Protectorate and poaches. Which pack are a group of rowdy morons who commit stupid acts of violence for fun. Who wants to murder another Garou for whatever motive. Who has frenzied and killed another Garou, but hid the body. Who is hanging out with vampires and making deals. Who is secretly aiding a group of Ronin. And so on.<br /> <br /> I admit that's more in theory than in practice. But having several ideas of criminals for NPCs and spreading them around your game is something I think adds to any chronicle. Too often these kind of NPCs are forgotten.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T13:03:18-07:00","id":1480122,"title":"","content":"Another source of inspiration are the relatively few werewolf themed TV shows that have existed over the years. There was brief TV show called Wolf Lake that aired in 2001 starring Lou Diamond Philips. It's not great, and it is easy to see why it was cancelled. But it had very good acting (Graham Greene, Tim Matheson, and Bruce McGill among others).<br /> <br /> It's basically about Lou Diamond Philips investigating a kinfolk community and gradually learning its secrets, and the internal conflicts within a Garou sept. There's a lot of things that can be taken by an ST to help them build their own kinfolk communities and internal conflicts.<br /> <br /> You can find the old episodes still on YouTube. <br /> <br /> I don't know if this was an actual TV promo or trailer, or fan made, but here is a trailer. (Unfortunately the show itself isn't as dramatic, mysterious, suspenseful, or action oriented as the trailer makes it out to be.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PHZnISyM6Wg\" data-code=\"PHZnISyM6Wg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PHZnISyM6Wg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> While I don't see any specific book, movie, or TV show to be definitive, there are enough media out there that can be mined for a lot of great inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T13:12:16-07:00","id":1480123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480119#post1480119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it won't. Delirium makes mortals forget crinos or rationalize it (&quot;it wasn't werewolf, these were terrorists&quot;) not forget about Garou in homid. The most optimistic version would be that such terrorists killed him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once more, why WOULD the garou stay in homid? Especially if it is their breed form. This is not a situation where the Veil really matters anyway.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> Yeah, survival cannibalism in situations you literally have no other choice I totally could see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T21:44:25-07:00","id":1480147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480123#post1480123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once more, why WOULD the garou stay in homid? Especially if it is their breed form. This is not a situation where the Veil really matters anyway.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Yeah, survival cannibalism in situations you literally have no other choice I totally could see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, try to imagine a trip on a plane. You can't fly in other form than homid. Maybe glabro. Assuming that you have time to prepare for a crash you still can't take other form (on the other hand hearing panic screams you should roll for frenzy but that would worsen the situation). If you don't frenzy there are two options. Either you remain conscious or not. If you are active you still have to walk away ignoring pleas for help if you don't want to be seen transforming. But others will propably interpret this as a state of shock and will try to stop you (another frenzy test?). If you are unconscious then you will be awoken by other survivors so they had seen your face and your disappearance will be seen as at least strange. And the Veil always matters. First of all it's one of the most important laws for Garou. And with the harshest punishement for breaking, regardless of the tribe. And second the shit can hit the fan even after many years, propably when you least expect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T10:51:47-07:00","id":1480184,"title":"","content":"A joke I've heard from Fianna:<br /> <br /> A Red Talon cub asks his father:<br /> - Daddy, why you have to circle a human a bit before you eat him?<br /> - If you like your food shit flavoured don't do that.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\ude09.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T13:59:43-07:00","id":1480205,"title":"","content":"Despite my love of the Red Talons and man eaters in the game, I actually don't have the Red Talons do much man eating when I ST chronicles. They have no problems killing humans. But since they see something as intrinsically wrong with mankind, they don't want to pollute themselves. Maybe they'll become mangy and lose their teeth. <br /> <br /> Sure, some Talons do eat the flesh of man, but no more than other tribes. But their reputation is such that it is a common belief or prejudice by the other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T14:38:20-07:00","id":1480209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480205#post1480205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite my love of the Red Talons and man eaters in the game, I actually don't have the Red Talons do much man eating when I ST chronicles. They have no problems killing humans. But since they see something as intrinsically wrong with mankind, they don't want to pollute themselves. Maybe they'll become mangy and lose their teeth.<br /> <br /> Sure, some Talons do eat the flesh of man, but no more than other tribes. But their reputation is such that it is a common belief or prejudice by the other tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it depends on where the Talons live. In more relaxed areas, they are less likely to go hog wild with bodies. But in areas with a lot of strife with humanity, they tend to get vicious. So in relaxed areas, they just kill the human, but in areas where they are driven to the edge they want REVENGE. Hence why Dying Cubs are a thing.<br /> <br /> The view on the Litany also varies. Some really do not bother with the 'we weren't there to decide on it' and just follow it as usual. To some, they feel slighted by the Nation for deciding without the Talons.<br /> <br /> (Even though Talons WERE invited, they just thought it was too human.)<br /> <br /> I go by the idea that the Talons are pretty laid back most of the time, as they are not a war tribe and wolves are pretty chill. Because I dislike the Raging Beast concept as the default for the tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:44:45-07:00","id":1480238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480209#post1480209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go by the idea that the Talons are pretty laid back most of the time, as they are not a war tribe and wolves are pretty chill. Because I dislike the Raging Beast concept as the default for the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't buy the Talon's usual description precisely because I can't see wolf-born buying so intensely an ideology that is ultimately human about &quot;natural purity&quot; when they finally understand the sapience that made them different from other wolves before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T23:42:18-07:00","id":1480266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479200-so-the-howling?p=1480238#post1480238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't buy the Talon's usual description precisely because I can't see wolf-born buying so intensely an ideology that is ultimately human about &quot;natural purity&quot; when they finally understand the sapience that made them different from other wolves before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, but because its both denial (going from wolf to human smarts is SCARY) and cultural. Talon culture HEAVILY focuses on pretending they are wolves, like, actively. To use a crude example, it is a bit like being in the closet. Only a bit, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}